; #GLOBALS - ALL WEAPON MODS# ===================================================================================================
; Name...........: $GC_AS_ALL_WEAPON_MODS
; Description....: Every token that can appear in a ModStruct should be listed here.
;                  This array feeds the token set ($g_m_AllMods) and the single-pass parser regex ($g_s_AllModsRegex).
; Shape..........: 1D array of strings, e.g. [ "FIRE_20_CAST","FIRE_20_RECH","+30_HP","-3_HEX","VAMP","ZEAL","15ALWAYS","E_REG", ... ]
; Used by........: ItemFilter_InitAllMods() → builds $g_m_AllMods (set) and $g_s_AllModsRegex (alternation).
; Configuration..: - Ensure every token used in any *_PATTERNS array is present here (normalized the same way).
;                  - Prefer unambiguous tokens (avoid substring overlaps); the parser mitigates via length-sorted regex,
;                    but unique tokens yield the best performance and correctness.
; Related........: ItemFilter_InitAllMods, ItemFilter_ParseModsFromStruct, ItemFilter_NormalizeMod
; ===============================================================================================================================
Global Const $GC_AS_ALL_WEAPON_MODS = [ _
	$GC_S_MOD_SHIELD_MINUS3_HEX, $GC_S_MOD_SHIELD_MINUS2_STANCE, $GC_S_MOD_SHIELD_MINUS2_ENCH, $GC_S_MOD_SHIELD_MINUS520, _
